Converted collection / variable[0].key [opencollection.yml]: the variable `base url` was renamed to `base_url`
Converted Users / Get user / request.url.raw [Users/Get user.yml]: the URL fragment `#frag` was removed
Renamed Users / a-b [Users/a-b 1.yml]: the name `a-b` cannot be used as a file name here, so it was written to `Users/a-b 1.yml`; the display name is kept
Converted Settings / request.auth.password [Settings.yml]: the value is kept as the secret variable `settings_password`, not in the file
Converted collection [opencollection.yml]: runs use the environment `Environment` by default, since it holds the imported credentials
Converted imported credentials [environments/Environment.yml]: the imported credentials are the secret variables `settings_password`; their values are kept in the secret store, not in the file
NeedsInput collection [-]: needs a value: `host`, `k`, `token`; nothing imported defines them, so add them to the collection's variables or an environment before sending
== Settings.yml
info:
  name: Settings
  type: http
  seq: 3

http:
  method: GET
  url: https://example.com/settings
  auth:
    type: basic
    username: u
    password: "{{settings_password}}"

settings:
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: inherit
  followRedirects: false
  maxRedirects: 3
  forwardAuthorizationHeader: true
== Users/Get user.yml
info:
  name: Get user
  type: http
  seq: 1

http:
  method: GET
  url: https://{{host}}/users/:id?expand=true&debug=1
  headers:
    - name: Accept
      value: application/json
      description: What we take
    - name: X-Off
      value: "1"
      disabled: true
  params:
    - name: expand
      value: "true"
      type: query
      description: Expand relations
    - name: debug
      value: "1"
      type: query
      disabled: true
    - name: id
      value: "42"
      type: path
      description: User id
  auth: inherit

settings:
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: inherit
  followRedirects: true
  maxRedirects: 5
  forwardAuthorizationHeader: false

docs: Fetches one user
